Can I pass `{ error: "not found" }` — object literal field with string value, fine. `{ status: 404 }` — fine.

The grammar requires TypeArgs in call: `Response.json({ ok: true })` — PostfixSuffix allows `TypeArgs? "(" [Args] ")"` so type args optional. Good.

One concern: `req.path` — is the field named `path`? The durable example uses `req.path === "/wait"` — yes. And `req.method` — yes.

Also the export: `export function handler` — allowed (FunctionDecl with export). Return type is a Type — `Proof<Response, "deterministic" | "state_isolated">` is NonTuplePrimaryType `Ident TypeArgs?` with union inside. Good — matches module examples.

